"suggestion":"1. Increase the contrast and saturation of the puzzle board elements (player, crate, lever, target) to make the grid the clear primary focal point, reducing the visual weight of the title. 2. Add a subtle glow or outline to the player character to establish them as the primary anchor. 3. Strengthen the visual link between the 'Objectives' list and the board by using matching iconography or color-coding (e.g., the 'Crate' objective icon should match the crate on the board exactly). 4. Group the 'Legend' and 'Controls' more tightly or move them to a collapsible section to reduce sidebar density and keep the focus on the 'Objectives' and the board. 5. Make the target pad more distinct (e.g., a solid outline or a different color) so it reads as a destination rather than a UI element."
