"critique": "The visual system suffers from a lack of geometric cohesion between the board and the UI chrome. The board uses a strict square grid, but the UI elements (HUD, side panels, buttons) utilize inconsistent corner radii (some are pill-shaped, others are rounded rectangles, and the board itself has a different radius), creating a fragmented 'component grammar.' The typography is inconsistent: the main title uses a high-contrast serif, while the HUD and body text use a monospace font, but the 'Objectives' and 'Legend' headers use a sans-serif or different weight that doesn't clearly align with either, causing visual noise. The 'Worker' character on the board is a flat 2D sprite that clashes with the 3D, beveled, and textured appearance of the crates, walls, and lever, making the board look like a collage of different art styles. The 'Target pad' on the board is a dashed outline, which is visually weak and inconsistent with the solid, material-heavy look of the rest of the environment. The color palette is muddy; the dark browns of the floor and walls have low contrast, making the grid lines and boundaries difficult to read, and the 'red' of the lever and exit door is a desaturated brick color that doesn't pop against the background.",
"suggestion": "1. Unify the component geometry: Establish a single corner radius (e.g., 8px or 12px) for all UI containers, buttons, and the board frame to create a consistent visual language. 2. Harmonize the art style: Redesign the 'Worker' character to match the 3D/beveled aesthetic of the crates and walls, or flatten the board elements to match the character. 3. Strengthen the 'Target pad': Replace the dashed outline with a solid, glowing, or textured surface that reads as a physical object on the floor, consistent with the 'pad' description. 4. Refine the typography: Choose a consistent typeface family for all UI text (excluding the title) and ensure clear hierarchy through weight and size rather than font switching. 5. Increase contrast: Lighten the floor tiles or darken the grid lines to make the board grid more legible. 6. Vibrant accents: Increase the saturation of the red elements (lever, exit door) to make them stand out as key interactive elements against the brown background."
